'''''Arceuthobium azoricum''''' ([[Portuguese language|Portuguese]]: '''espigos-de-cedro''') is a species of [[dwarf mistletoe]] [[endemic]] to the [[Azores]]. The population is restricted to the ''Grupo Central'' (central group) of the archipelago on [[Faial Island|Faial]], [[Pico Island|Pico]], [[São Jorge Island|São Jorge]] and [[Terceira]] islands. It is a [[parasitic plant]] of the local ''[[Juniperus brevifolia]]''.<ref>{{cite web |title=Arceuthobium azoricum |url=https://acores.flora-on.pt/#/1Arceuthobium+azoricum |publisher=flora-on |accessdate=22 October 2020}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Species Details: Arceuthobium azoricum D. Wiens & F. G. Hawksworth |url=http://www.catalogueoflife.org/col/details/species/id/7833924d22c7d6c2d1c52cbc2758ca33 |website=www.catalogueoflife.org |publisher=Catalogue of Life |accessdate=22 October 2020}}</ref>

